-   entry .encodable   the `<svg>` element with its definitions and figures, as `svg.in[Xml]`
-   entry .aggregable   `text.read[Svg]`: parses SVG text, discarding any XML declaration before the element
-       Needs `Tactic[Parse.Error]`, `Tactic[Xml.Error]` and `Tactic[Svg.Error]` in scope. The
-       XML is parsed against `XmlSchema.Freeform`, so the caller gives no schema.
-   entry .loadable   `text.load[Svg]`: a `Document[Svg]` whose metadata is the declared encoding
-       Needs the same three tactics. The encoding defaults to UTF-8 when none is declared.
-   entry .loadableData   `data.load[Svg]`: a `Document[Svg]` parsed from bytes
-       Needs the three tactics and a `Buffering` in scope.
-   entry .showable   a `Document[Svg]` as a standalone file: the XML declaration, then the element
-       `Document(Svg(10, 10), enc"UTF-8").show` begins `<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>`.
-   entry .Error   raised when SVG text cannot be read as an `Svg`
