-     entry #ops   the path operations, most recent first
-     entry #style   the inline CSS, or `Unset`
-     entry #id   the identifier, or `Unset`
-     entry #transforms   the transforms, written as the `transform` attribute
-     entry #moveTo   `M`: a move to an absolute point
-     entry #lineTo   `L`: a line to an absolute point
-     entry #move   `m`: a move by a `Delta`
-     entry #line   `l`, `h` or `v`: a line by a `Delta`, written as `h` or `v` when it is along one axis
-     entry #curve   `c` or `s`: a relative cubic curve, with both control points or only the second
-         `curve(ctrl1, ctrl2, point)` is a full cubic; `curve(ctrl2, point)` continues smoothly
-         from the previous curve, the first control point reflected.
-     entry #curveTo   `C` or `S`: an absolute cubic curve, with both control points or only the second
-     entry #quadCurve   `q` or `t`: a relative quadratic curve, with its control point or continuing smoothly
-     entry #quadCurveTo   `Q` or `T`: an absolute quadratic curve, with its control point or continuing smoothly
-     entry #moveUp   a relative move written as `Move(Delta(0, -value))`
-     entry #moveDown   a relative move written as `Move(Delta(0, value))`
-     entry #moveLeft   a relative move written as `Move(Delta(-value, 0))`
-     entry #moveRight   a relative move written as `Move(Delta(value, 0))`
-     entry #lineUp   a relative line written as `Draw(Delta(0, -value))`, rendered `v -value`
-     entry #lineDown   a relative line written as `Draw(Delta(0, value))`, rendered `v value`
-     entry #lineLeft   a relative line written as `Draw(Delta(-value, 0))`, rendered `h -value`
-     entry #lineRight   a relative line written as `Draw(Delta(value, 0))`, rendered `h value`
-     entry #closed   `Z`: closes the current subpath back to its start
-   entry .Ellipse   an `<ellipse>`, or a `<circle>` when its radii are equal
